      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=3{log}_{4}⁡(x)+2?$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot $y=3{log}_{4}⁡(x)+2,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y={log}_{4}⁡(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270407/assets/b557682d2648618f63c554a5e591a1b1e639a7b13116b86459170b2121aa5614.png)\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=3{log}_{4}⁡(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270407/assets/52d4177f6499fbafbc34972fe000a12b2bb125526ed95c855bb179ae458bb17c.png)\n\n- Then, translate the result by $2$ units up to get the graph of $y=3{log}_{4}⁡(x)+2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270407/assets/20a8a8aca209528f4d8e7656bb344c4bf1456eaeaf407bf71ff1dcba982a9bf6.png)",
